  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Supreme Court of India recently issued a significant order regarding legal petitions and institutional oversight. The court set aside a previous directive from the Allahabad High Court that had called for inquiries by the Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) and the Enforcement Directorate (ED) into alleged disproportionate assets associated with Congress leader Rahul Gandhi. In its ruling, the Supreme Court specified that Rahul Gandhi must be impleaded as a party in the relevant High Court case to ensure proper legal process. This development follows a period of active judicial intervention by the Supreme Court across various national legal matters, ranging from the review of election-related laws and local election administration to the oversight of criminal bail guidelines and environmental policy implementation in urban areas.",
